[REF] sale(_management): replace optional products with optional sections

Before this commit, optional products were managed through the separate models
`sale.order.option` and `sale.order.template.option`, displayed in a dedicated
"Optional Products" tab on the sale order form.

This commit removes those models and introduces the concept of optional sections
allowing any section or subsection to be marked as optional directly from the
section dropdown.

Key changes:
* Any section/subsection can be marked as optional.
* When marked, all product lines beneath it have their quantities set to `0`.
* Products in optional sections remain editable for both portal users and admins
* A product in an optional section with quantity `1` is considered as opted in.

This unifies product and optional product handling, improving usability and
portal interaction.

